 disrupting this one, who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T16:18:09-08:00","id":1350724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1350375#post1350375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order for the Exarchs to have been mages who Ascended their way into Tyranny symbols, there has to be a reality in which they weren't, a reality no longer available in any way, shape, or form-but it's the question mark of whether the Judges existed in that question mark that is worth noting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the distinction meaningful? On some level it depends on metaphysical primacy of course, but consider a possible state of affairs:<br /> <br /> World that was: Judges exist in some form. Exarchs are moral mages who ascend.<br /> <br /> World that is: The Tyranny symbols of the exarchs are burned into reality from its utter beginning to its final end. The Judges are created as written. Their cruelty and the Law of Suffering which are fundamental to their being from their creation are reflections of/arise from the shadows of the Exarchs. The Judges have no knowledge of the world that was and might not even recognize those Judges that Were.<br /> <br /> <br /> As I understood it, changes in the Supernal alter all realms of existence except those in the Supernal itself or within the souls of archmages. Even if such changes don't directly affect other realms, the changes they impose on the world necessarily has backwash effects on Realms so fundamentally tied with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 11-24-2019, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T16:41:48-08:00","id":1350729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1350724#post1350724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is the distinction meaningful? On some level it depends on metaphysical primacy of course, but consider a possible state of affairs:<br /> <br /> World that was: Judges exist in some form. Exarchs are moral mages who ascend.<br /> <br /> World that is: The Tyranny symbols of the exarchs are burned into reality from its utter beginning to its final end. The Judges are created as written. Their cruelty and the Law of Suffering which are fundamental to their being from their creation are reflections of/arise from the shadows of the Exarchs. The Judges have no knowledge of the world that was and might not even recognize those Judges that Were.<br /> <br /> <br /> As I understood it, changes in the Supernal alter all realms of existence except those in the Supernal itself or within the souls of archmages. Even if such changes don't directly affect other realms, the changes they impose on the world necessarily has backwash effects on Realms so fundamentally tied with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is like asking if Ruins of the Time Before are meaningful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T16:58:28-08:00","id":1350734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1350729#post1350729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is like asking if Ruins of the Time Before are meaningful.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't though. The Ruins might be useful, but at this point what makes the Exarchs different from any other Supernal symbol which predated them? (In so much as predate is a meaningful term in the Supernal where Time is itself defined)<br /> <br /> Newly ascended Archmasters have this same problem after their own ascension. If the people in their lives have not only no memory but no causal influence from the Archmaster, are they the same people? Is the Archmaster entitled to any sort of relationship because they remember a timeline these people weren't part of?<br /> <br /> If the Judges Before were compassionate arbiters who created the Law of Sufferance that said all life could do what it wanted if it didn't bother other life, will overwhelming and conclusive evidence of that make any of the current Judges a fraction less assholish?<br /> <br /> Yes, perhaps the Judges are exactly what they say they are. But what they say they are and what they used to be could be as different as what the Exarchs say they are and what they used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T17:13:08-08:00","id":1350736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1350724#post1350724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the distinction meaningful?</div> </div> </div> </div>Moreso when talking on the forums than playing the game.<br /> <br /> These things can have an impact on a setting, and clearly attract attention (you'll note several hundred pages of posts arguing about the cosmology of any setting, and not nearly as much dedicated to player characters), but the games are mostly focused on the here and now (or in the case of Mummy here and there, now and then).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-24-2019, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T20:16:39-08:00","id":1351776,"title":"","content":"Any new interest in this now that we've seen how the Judges manifest in the world?<br /> <br /> Any chance of not derailing this thread based on the <i>hypothetical</i> nature of the Exarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T23:19:00-08:00","id":1351797,"title":"","content":"I <i>still</i> not got answer if Judges are more like Great Old Ones - or Idigama...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-30-2019, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T23:54:11-08:00","id":1351802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1351797#post1351797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I STILL sis not got answer if Judges are more like Great Old Ones - or Idigama...</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither.<br /> <br /> The Judges are a step (or a step and a half) below omnipresent cosmic forces like creation, destruction, and manifest existence, second only to the defiance and unpredictability of all things. They are foundational to ordered reality as experienced in Mummy: the Curse, and it is this closeness to root divinity that likely makes their described appearances and physical manifestations so terrifying.<br /> <br /> Derived from this, they are a set of forty-two <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">THOU SHALT NOT</span>s that Irem's legacy of civilization is built upon, serving as channels for the Devourer to receive her tithe of souls, because they do not care for the world they judge except insofar as they are compelled to by their place in the cosmos. They are cruel and their place in the cosmos specifically includes &quot;humans are important, because they're the only things we're allowed to feed to Ammut so she'll let the universe at large continue to exist,&quot; which I am given to understand is kind of the opposite of how that power dynamic usually manifests for the Great Old Ones.<br /> <br /> They are likewise not terribly close to the shifting proto-symbolic entities that are the idigam, who can certainly have a passive impact on the world around them as spiritual beings, but who lack the occult grounding one expects from something reality itself is built on; the idigam's creative approach to reality stems mostly from attempts to define new concepts, which makes them extremely late to the game as far as primordial beings go.<br /> <br /> The Judges are sharp edges on the rock of coherent reality, and the world theoretically dances to their tune because the song they're playing is stimulus-response that they refined into specific forbiddances at some point thousands of years ago. They're not disinterested in our world, and if their emergence from chaos has any truth to it it's so far in the relative past as to be irrelevant to anyone not banking on an objective and eternal order to the cosmos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T14:45:43-08:00","id":1351916,"title":"","content":"I suddenly realized that the theoretical &quot;nice guy&quot; judges ya'll are talking about are basically what we had in Mummy: the Resurrection, and I don't know how to feel about that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T15:43:42-08:00","id":1351921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1351797#post1351797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>still</i> not got answer if Judges are more like Great Old Ones - or Idigama...</div> </div> </div> </div>I openly told you the answer to this on the first page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T19:33:39-08:00","id":1351950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1351916#post1351916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suddenly realized that the theoretical &quot;nice guy&quot; judges ya'll are talking about are basically what we had in Mummy: the Resurrection, and I don't know how to feel about that...</div> </div> </div> </div>I miss the nice guy judges and the nice guy mummies of Resurrection, so if anything brings even portions of that back as a potential I am all for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T20:07:36-08:00","id":1351953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1351797#post1351797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>still</i> not got answer if Judges are more like Great Old Ones - or Idigama...</div> </div> </div> </div>You've been here long enough to know that you are not going to get an answer about it on the forums from developers or writers (on the project), especially during a Kickstarter when someone can decide they don't like the answer and yank their pledge. You can make your own decisions about the matter after reading the manuscript/book, like everyone else.<br /> <br /> Then you can tell them they're wrong for not agreeing with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-30-2019, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T23:25:39-08:00","id":1351973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1351953#post1351953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you can tell them they're wrong for not agreeing with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>As is the tradition! ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T07:42:00-08:00","id":1352009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1351797#post1351797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>still</i> not got answer if Judges are more like Great Old Ones - or Idigama...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The answer is no, they aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T18:33:20-08:00","id":1353197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1351802#post1351802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;humans are important, because they're the only things we're allowed to feed to Ammut so she'll let the universe at large continue to exist,&quot; which I am given to understand is kind of the opposite of how that power dynamic usually manifests for the Great Old Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, they believe she'll destroy the world if they're not allowed to feed enough souls to her?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T18:52:23-08:00","id":1353201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353197#post1353197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, they believe she'll destroy the world if they're not allowed to feed enough souls to her?</div> </div> </div> </div>Between the accounts presented in Dreams, the account presented by the Deceived temakh, and the simple fact that she made the Shuankhsen out of people the Shan'iatu gave her as sacrificial victims? Hell yes, she's a greedy, greedy goddess of the devouring ages.<br /> <br /> It could well be that she's no longer placed to eat the world in one gulp the way myth poses her as being capable of at the dawn of the world, but Sutek and the Judges both call her &quot;necessary&quot; in a way that's used as a framing for appeasement and she's definitely proved herself motivated to pursue Sekhem beyond what she was promised even as she stays her jaws for the Arisen to fulfill their twofold purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T19:38:25-08:00","id":1353219,"title":"","content":"Is the total amount of Sekhem fixed, or does the proliferation of life create more of it? The Judges wanted to get it over with in a lump sum, but might Sutek's &quot;wager&quot; offer the possibility of more Sekhem for Ammut in the long run than if she had just eaten the world in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T19:51:44-08:00","id":1353224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353219#post1353219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the total amount of Sekhem fixed, or does the proliferation of life create more of it? The Judges wanted to get it over with in a lump sum, but might Sutek's &quot;wager&quot; offer the possibility of more Sekhem for Ammut in the long run than if she had just eaten the world in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lump sum of an ill defined 10%.<br /> <br /> Ammut doesn't need an amount-her problem is, as mythically displayed, she's got a rock in her mouth with a lot of complaining people on it. The Sekhem is a perk to keeping the rock in her mouth, but if she doesn't get enough to warrant the hassle of a rock in her mouth, well then.<br /> <br /> Chomp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T19:54:23-08:00","id":1353225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353219#post1353219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the total amount of Sekhem fixed, or does the proliferation of life create more of it? The Judges wanted to get it over with in a lump sum, but might Sutek's &quot;wager&quot; offer the possibility of more Sekhem for Ammut in the long run than if she had just eaten the world in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Open question, particularly given certain story seeds provided in 2e, but it's important to remember that Sekhem is secondary to Ammut's actual desire and she has no qualms with pursuing that desire outside the bounds of any bargains offered to her; what the Judges offered her before Sutek's decree was as much a compromise as what they offered after.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Meet me in the middle,&quot; says the unjust man.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T20:48:17-08:00","id":1353236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353224#post1353224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lump sum of an ill defined 10%.<br /> <br /> Ammut doesn't need an amount-her problem is, as mythically displayed, she's got a rock in her mouth with a lot of complaining people on it. The Sekhem is a perk to keeping the rock in her mouth, but if she doesn't get enough to warrant the hassle of a rock in her mouth, well then.<br /> <br /> Chomp.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't really an answer. Because if having a rock in her mouth is so unpleasant and Sekhem at all desirable, then she could just swallow it, get all the Sekhem, and be done with the annoyance.<br /> <br /> So the broader question is: What is she getting out of this deal that actually makes it worth her while to keep up her end? I had the suspicion that by holding off she was increasing the total amount of what she got (cheating aside), much like fattening cattle before slaughtering them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 12-06-2019, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T21:03:04-08:00","id":1353239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353236#post1353236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't really an answer. Because if having a rock in her mouth is so unpleasant and Sekhem at all desirable, then she could just swallow it, get all the Sekhem, and be done with the annoyance.<br /> <br /> So the broader question is: What is she getting out of this deal that actually makes it worth her while to keep up her end?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sekhem is, among other things, a motion, a kinetic energy.<br /> <br /> The rock is potential energy.<br /> <br /> Chomping down on the potential energy does not yield that kinetic energy.<br /> <br /> On a different angle, Sekhem is....flavor. It's taste. It's savory, sweet, sour, bitter, salty. The rock remains, by itself, a rock-but Sekhem is the spice that makes everything flavorful. You don't kill your favorite chefs until they stop performing to standard.<br /> <br /> The second to final point if you're questioning the motives an annihilation/temptation goddess as though it were a rational human being who somehow <i>needs</i> motivation instead of simply <i>existing</i> in a capacity that doesn't fuck everything over until myriad other circumstances come into play.<br /> <br /> She's a goddess-an abstract concept given actualization in reality through mysterious occult forms, forces, and means. She doesn't, ultimately, <i>need anything</i>.<br /> <br /> Which leads to the final point*, a tinge of the cosmic horror to reconcile with: Truth be told, she <i>doesn't</i> need or even necessarily <i>want</i> any of this shit. Whatever her reasons for maintaining it, it's secondary to the fact that she doesn't need it. Who cares <i>why, </i>when at the end of the day, She could<br /> <br /> just<br /> <br /> decide to say fuck it.<br /> <br /> And that's all she chewed.<br /> <br /> *Okay, I say that, but as I write it, I recall the binding of Atum that occurs as Ammut reveals herself-it's like a footnote in the grand scheme of what ultimately matters for Curse's themes and story, because Ammut's inevitable victory over reality is non-concerned with reality as people deal with it-but I'll pour over Dreams again on that section to see if there's a factor that matters.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, she's entropy. She doesn't need anything, but tolerates reality at it's own self-destructive pace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T21:10:25-08:00","id":1353241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353236#post1353236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the broader question is: What is she getting out of this deal that actually makes it worth her while to keep up her end?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ending things is what she does, and she's good at it and enjoys it a great deal.<br /> <br /> Her endgame is The Complete Cessation Of Everything Forever, but the world is too structured for her to manifest directly anymore, the Judges are useful to her purposes by their being so prepared to compromise and drive the rest of Creation to her embrace directly or indirectly, and everything that exists inherited Will from Sutek, who inherited from Atum, her opposite number in the big three primordial forces of Irem's creation myth.<br /> <br /> So she's stuck playing the long game; to borrow an analogous scheme from Changeling's Morphean the Rogue Sister, she's down to making deals to kill other deals. Without the legroom to just sweep in past the horizon and crunch the rock in one go, she's settled for subverting Creation to end Creation one step at a time.<br /> <br /> She has eternity to play with, after all \u2014 once a relic's Sekhem is consigned to Duat, it remains there until and unless the Judges deign to send it back, which puts it on the playing field again for the Devourer to consume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T21:13:58-08:00","id":1353243,"title":"","content":"I would like to also note that this is a cosmology where the first deity ever didn't exist until it basically wondered when it would exist at which point the wondering spawned another deity who then spawned the first deity.<br /> <br /> Casual and causal logic is a dead hunk of flesh where mythology is concerned, and the world of Curse is nothing if not mythological.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-07-2019, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T21:35:24-08:00","id":1353247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353197#post1353197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, they believe she'll destroy the world if they're not allowed to feed enough souls to her?</div> </div> </div> </div>To answer this more directly with a quote now that I'm not on mobile:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Judges and Shan'iatu, Translator's Introduction</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should also note the role of Iremite theodicy. Suffering drives life to change, act, and adapt, and is part of the basic makeup of the Judges\u2019 cosmos. <b>Creation legends say that Ammut must be appeased or she\u2019ll consume everything.</b> The Judges were willing to simply consign a portion of Creation to oblivion, but Sutek asserted that only beings capable of disobeying the Law of Suffering are appropriate sacrifices. If they choose the path the Heretic calls \u201cWill,\u201d they can rise to a place beside the Judges, in heavenly A\u2019aru. Otherwise, they go to Duat.<br /> <br /> <b>Humanity needed to be educated and brought up to the task of choosing, but the Judges didn\u2019t want to make it too easy to choose A\u2019aru, lest they starve and enrage the Devourer.</b> Thus, note that some of the commands given to the temakhs are paradoxical, or even hypocritical. The Judges command them to deceive humans but punish liars, for example. Some of the Judges issue straightforward directives, but many seem to demand that their servants actively tempt mortals to commit sins worth punishing. Perhaps this explains why, after becoming the Shan\u2019iatu of Irem, the temakhs pursued the cruel, despotic rule the Heretic remembers.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T23:56:15-08:00","id":1353264,"title":"","content":"Ah, that would account for why there\u2019s a Judge dedicated to punishing the sin of enslaving and oppressing others, despite literally everything we know about Irem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T11:00:50-08:00","id":1353387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353197#post1353197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, they believe she'll destroy the world if they're not allowed to feed enough souls to her?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See Dreams of Avarice for this and more on Irem creation myths and the path of Apotheosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T11:17:07-08:00","id":1353389,"title":"","content":"Also, as a practical matter the Devourer is smart enough to know that it is hunger incarnate. It maybe could devour all existence....and tomorrow it would still be hungry and have nothing to eat. Devouring a piece at a time makes more sense even if it is less momentarily satisfying than it would be to feast all all things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T07:16:09-08:00","id":1353830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1351802#post1351802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Idigam or Old One?] Neither.<br /> <br /> The Judges are a step (or a step and a half) below omnipresent cosmic forces like creation, destruction, and manifest existence, second only to the defiance and unpredictability of all things. They are foundational to ordered reality as experienced in Mummy: the Curse, and it is this closeness to root divinity that likely makes their described appearances and physical manifestations so terrifying.<br /> <br /> Derived from this, they are a set of forty-two <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">THOU SHALT NOT</span>s that Irem's legacy of civilization is built upon, serving as channels for the Devourer to receive her tithe of souls, because they do not care for the world they judge except insofar as they are compelled to by their place in the cosmos. They are cruel and their place in the cosmos specifically includes &quot;humans are important, because they're the only things we're allowed to feed to Ammut so she'll let the universe at large continue to exist,&quot; which I am given to understand is kind of the opposite of how that power dynamic usually manifests for the Great Old Ones.<br /> <br /> They are likewise not terribly close to the shifting proto-symbolic entities that are the idigam, who can certainly have a passive impact on the world around them as spiritual beings, but who lack the occult grounding one expects from something reality itself is built on; the idigam's creative approach to reality stems mostly from attempts to define new concepts, which makes them extremely late to the game as far as primordial beings go.<br /> <br /> The Judges are sharp edges on the rock of coherent reality, and the world theoretically dances to their tune because the song they're playing is stimulus-response that they refined into specific forbiddances at some point thousands of years ago. They're not disinterested in our world, and if their emergence from chaos has any truth to it it's so far in the relative past as to be irrelevant to anyone not banking on an objective and eternal order to the cosmos.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two fundamentally terrifying sides of the coin of horror: the thing that is very interested in you that you do not understand, and the thing that is very DIS-interested in you that you do not understand. (Assumption: you are impacted in both cases. Otherwise, there is no conflict and thus no horror.)<br /> <br /> Acknowledging that the Judges are side 1. What do we have in CofD cosmology that most closely fits side 2 and thus either are or could be scaled into the Great Old One eldritch horrors of Lovecraftian fame?<br /> <br /> (Mummy's emphasis on cults can induce senses of Lovecraft, but cults could show up in any gameline, so let's set that aside.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T07:47:52-08:00","id":1353836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353830#post1353830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acknowledging that the Judges are side 1. What do we have in CofD cosmology that most closely fits side 2 and thus either are or could be scaled into the Great Old One eldritch horrors of Lovecraftian fame?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a pat simplification in general, but the Annunaki presumably have a similar relation to the world as the True Fae do: just like not all of the Gentry manifest their Titles as Keepers and other forms intent upon some stolen element of the waking world, much (inasmuch as &quot;much&quot; means anything in a place where quantity doesn't really exist) of the Abyss seems unconcerned with material reality unless it bothers them; that the hostility of the Abyss appears to have increased from the perspective of linear time as the Phenomenal World's history has moved on could be sampling bias or it could be indicative of the reality-hating elements of the Abyss getting more of their tendrils in the Tapestry, but for the most part the default state of an Abyssal entity in its normal state seems to be indifference to the world generated by the Supernal.<br /> <br /> By a similar tone, albeit at a reduced scale, the chthonians of Geist explicitly don't care about the ghosts around them unless they've stumbled into a hunting ground somewhere on the Rivers or elsewhere, being largely content to just eat each other and filter feed on the Essence carried down from the living world. No verdict yet on whether the Chthonic Gods (should they really exist) have any direct relation to the never-born &quot;natives&quot; of the Underworld, but the directive they impose upon Reapers is sufficiently interested-in-people that it somewhat outweighs their mythic scope.<br /> <br /> And then there's Weird Shit In The Anima Mundi, for which &quot;psychic superbeings from the dreams of the world itself&quot; initially sounds comprehensible until you remember that it's the source of a couple particularly worrying Legacies like the Unforgotten Scions and the Morphean Continuity; there's things in the Dreamtime that humanity only has tenuous terminology for, and many of them are content to go about their business beyond the Omphalos without ever seeing human contact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T09:33:08-08:00","id":1353869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353836#post1353836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>It's a pat simplification in general</b>, but the Annunaki presumably have a similar relation to the world as the True Fae do: just like not all of the Gentry manifest their Titles as Keepers and other forms intent upon some stolen element of the waking world, much (inasmuch as &quot;much&quot; means anything in a place where quantity doesn't really exist) of the Abyss seems unconcerned with material reality unless it bothers them; that the hostility of the Abyss appears to have increased from the perspective of linear time as the Phenomenal World's history has moved on could be sampling bias or it could be indicative of the reality-hating elements of the Abyss getting more of their tendrils in the Tapestry, but for the most part the default state of an Abyssal entity in its normal state seems to be indifference to the world generated by the Supernal.<br /> <br /> By a similar tone, albeit at a reduced scale, the chthonians of Geist explicitly don't care about the ghosts around them unless they've stumbled into a hunting ground somewhere on the Rivers or elsewhere, being largely content to just eat each other and filter feed on the Essence carried down from the living world. No verdict yet on whether the Chthonic Gods (should they really exist) have any direct relation to the never-born &quot;natives&quot; of the Underworld, but the directive they impose upon Reapers is sufficiently interested-in-people that it somewhat outweighs their mythic scope.<br /> <br /> And then there's Weird Shit In The Anima Mundi, for which &quot;psychic superbeings from the dreams of the world itself&quot; initially sounds comprehensible until you remember that it's the source of a couple particularly worrying Legacies like the Unforgotten Scions and the Morphean Continuity; there's things in the Dreamtime that humanity only has tenuous terminology for, and many of them are content to go about their business beyond the Omphalos without ever seeing human contact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Satchel. It's a pat simplification to attempt to jam down unknowable entities into knowable game systems (or at least mythology)--but we'll do it!<br /> <br /> I'm not an expert on Lovecraft, Mythos or the well-regarded games that utilize them, so if you'll humor me a moment I'll toss out a few names and maybe you all might suggest which broad bucket they might fall into? I'll do further research based on targeting.<br /> <br /> * Shub-Niggurath<br /> * Yog-Sothoth<br /> * King in Yellow (ok, Chambers not Lovecraft)<br /> <br /> While a few of the Mythos creations are in fact oblivious to man's sentience, others seem quite engaged and have distinctly Egyptian themes to them. These seem like good attributions to Judges in my quite novice eye.<br /> <br /> The ones above are harder, however.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T12:02:16-08:00","id":1353919,"title":"","content":"The Mythos isn't entirely staffed with entities that are unconcerned with humanity. The Migo go out of their way to harvest brains for example. And Narlehotep looks like a human and goes around doing wonder-shows for humans. Perhaps more disturbing is the possibility that Narlehotep doesn't look like humans but that humans look like Narlehotep and that if they go out into space and meet other civilizations <i>we</i> will be the ones that resemble cosmic horrors. <i>Or perhaps even be them to others</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T12:07:15-08:00","id":1353922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353919#post1353919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mythos isn't entirely staffed with entities that are unconcerned with humanity. The Migo go out of their way to harvest brains for example. And Narlehotep looks like a human and goes around doing wonder-shows for humans. Perhaps more disturbing is the possibility that Narlehotep doesn't look like humans but that humans look like Narlehotep and that if they go out into space and meet other civilizations <i>we</i> will be the ones that resemble cosmic horrors. <i>Or perhaps even be them to others</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <i>can</i> look like a human; a lot of Nyarlathotep's forms very much aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T09:59:13-08:00","id":1354189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353919#post1353919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps more disturbing is the possibility that Narlehotep doesn't look like humans but that humans look like Narlehotep and that if they go out into space and meet other civilizations <i>we</i> will be the ones that resemble cosmic horrors. <i>Or perhaps even be them to others</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangental, but relevant to the concept of the cosmic horror of the Other:<br /> <br /> Years ago there was a series of probably YA sci-fi books in which the alien races were all herbivorous, innately peaceful creatures because the predatorial, conflict-driven ones immolate themselves prior to achieving superluminal travel. Man is encountered by a collective of such aliens that happens to be locked into a losing war with a (also herbivorous) psychic slaver alien race.<br /> <br /> They decide the risks of using Man are worth it and hire humans as mercenaries. The results are hilarious, since even the (volunteer, trained, armed) females have such highly-developed predatory instincts, optimized muscle and bone density and other violent adaptations that they tear enemy platoons to shreds. The larger, even more aggressive male humans are such a savage terror on the battlefield (and off it) that they leave the collective almost wetting themselves.<br /> <br /> It was both an amusing and sobering look at Man.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T12:31:16-08:00","id":1354230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1354189#post1354189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tangental, but relevant to the concept of the cosmic horror of the Other:<br /> <br /> Years ago there was a series of probably YA sci-fi books in which the alien races were all herbivorous, innately peaceful creatures because the predatorial, conflict-driven ones immolate themselves prior to achieving superluminal travel. Man is encountered by a collective of such aliens that happens to be locked into a losing war with a (also herbivorous) psychic slaver alien race.<br /> <br /> They decide the risks of using Man are worth it and hire humans as mercenaries. The results are hilarious, since even the (volunteer, trained, armed) females have such highly-developed predatory instincts, optimized muscle and bone density and other violent adaptations that they tear enemy platoons to shreds. The larger, even more aggressive male humans are such a savage terror on the battlefield (and off it) that they leave the collective almost wetting themselves.<br /> <br /> It was both an amusing and sobering look at Man.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You may be thinking of the Damned Trilogy by Alan Dean Foster. If so, it wasn't just the females, but old ladies. The first human the aliens got into contact with was trying to keep humanity out of the war so chose the worst group of initial volunteers they could find. They all came back having loved the experience and doing disturbingly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T10:39:10-08:00","id":1354410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1354230#post1354230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You may be thinking of the Damned Trilogy by Alan Dean Foster. If so, it wasn't just the females, but old ladies. The first human the aliens got into contact with was trying to keep humanity out of the war so chose the worst group of initial volunteers they could find. They all came back having loved the experience and doing disturbingly well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's it exactly. Thanks!<br /> <br /> An overt plot point is the question: &quot;Once your alien monster has won the war for you, what do you do with it?&quot;<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}